WEBVTT

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:10.320
Eugen!

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.460
Where the heck did you go, Eugen?

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.940
I want to become a helmsman, see.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.030
But that's not all.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:03.000
I will make my dream come true. Promise!

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:24.810
Rackam.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:26.520
Rackam!

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:30.560
Huh? Something wrong, Gran?

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.940
You're not acting like your usual self.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.690
So I, uh, thought that something happened, maybe.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:40.660
Oh, nah. I've just been having
these bad dreams.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:41.620
That's all.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:47.710
We're getting close.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.260
That's Golonzo.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.620
What's the deal with that huge crane?

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.250
This place is packed with airships!

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:00.010
Are they all here on the island
to undergo repairs?

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:04.000
Yeah, but the engineers here
don't stop at maintenance and repairs.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.890
They can build you a whole ship to boot.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:08.760
Oh, yeah?

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:12.980
Indeed, this island plays host
to the best shipyards in the sky.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.110
Hey, Eugen!

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.480
Hey. 'Fraid I've got a job for ya.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:24.570
Are you... Rackam?

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.910
H-Hey.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.580
Well, blow me down!

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.700
Look what a fine man you've grown up to be!

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.460
That little kid who used
to tag along behind Eugen...

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:37.330
Hey, hey! Talk about ancient history!

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:41.960
Oh? So even Rackam was
a sweet little boy once!

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:47.090
"I'm gonna fix the Grandcypher!
I wanna go to Golonzo no matter what! Take me there!"

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:49.100
He was in tears, begging me.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:53.350
Yeah, he was always sniveling.
Getting lost all the time and stuff.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.440
Oh?

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:58.440
Good grief, I can't wait
to get off this stinking island.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.700
Looks like you had to go through hell to get here.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:07.780
I'm amazed that you were able to fly this far at all.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.660
It was a helmsman's skill
that got it here in one piece.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.460
Rackam, you did good!

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:17.420
Never mind that, how much will this cost?

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.840
Oh, right, let's see...

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:24.260
A couple of days for repairs,
and the cost should be, roughly...

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.130
Something like this.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:33.180
Um, one, ten, hundred, thousand...

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:34.890
Th-This much?

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.190
Hey, hey, it's not like I'm gouging you!

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:42.320
I know that. Well, I'd say that's reasonable.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.150
But...

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:47.280
Look here, he says he's going
to help out with the repairs.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:52.450
So you think you could knock a little off,
for old time's sake? Please?

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:57.160
If it were anyone else, Eugen...

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.210
All right!

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.590
To commemorate Rackam's triumphant return...

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:02.710
How's this?

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.210
We owe you big time!

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:09.840
We're grateful.
Still, that's a hefty expense.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:14.060
If that's the case...

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.520
I have a lucrative job you might like!

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:19.850
Sierokarte!

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:23.320
Long time no see, everybody.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.820
I'm glad that you're all looking well!

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.150
You look as well as ever yourself, Sierokarte.

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:30.700
Popping up out of nowhere, as usual!

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.450
So what kind of job is it?

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.080
Right!

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:39.580
Fortunately, I'm swamped with requests,
and I'm just so short-staffed!

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:44.210
If you could take on this job, it would help a lot.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:45.880
What do you think?

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:46.460
- Please let us do it!
- We'll do it!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.840
I guess this is what
"getting what you wish for" means.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:53.600
All right, I'm gonna stay behind
and get started on the repairs.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.350
You guys go out and
make us some serious money, okay?

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:01.350
All right! Let's give it our all for the Grandcypher!

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.110
Right!

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:05.190
All that's left is the contract, right?

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.400
Huh? Oh, that.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.450
No need for anything like that!

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:13.280
Don't worry, I'll get it done, all right?

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:17.290
Are you sure about this?

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:19.790
Sure. Here in Golonzo...

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.500
This is how things are done.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:28.670
There's a legend about a god who's been
enforcing promises on this island since ancient times.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:34.680
Even in the case of verbal promises,
no one has ever reneged, not once.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.560
Yeah, but...

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:41.270
That's just a legend, right?

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:45.060
It might be a primal beast.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:49.860
Ever since we got to this island,
I've been sensing a primal beast's power.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.610
A primal beast on Golonzo, too?

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:54.570
Yes.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.330
Enforcing promises...

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:01.210
Perhaps a primal beast that governs contracts?

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:05.710
Then we can't make any casual
or offbeat promises on this island, huh?

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:10.340
Right. If we make any outrageous promises
without thinking, it could mean trouble.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.090
Right.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:17.600
It'll cost you, but I've got some
cutting-edge materials, quality stuff.

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:18.810
Wanna try 'em out?

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.520
No, the same stuff will do.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:26.360
Could effect our balance if the weight changes.
Now I just need...

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:33.490
You've joined a top of the line...
No, an elite crew, haven't you, Rackam?

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:35.870
Life must be smooth sailing for you, huh?

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:36.450
Huh?

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:41.580
A man with your skills,
I bet you could find a job anywhere.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.290
So what are your plans?

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:47.460
You could show off your mastery in
a skyfaring crew renowned throughout the skies!

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:51.170
Or you could become a freewheeling traveler,
just you and your ship!

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:55.680
Any man would kill to live that life
just once, am I right?

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:58.180
No, I don't really...

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:00.010
Whoa, my bad, my bad.

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:02.180
Guess that was uncalled for, huh?

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:07.770
After all, a guy like you
must've decided your future long ago, eh?

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:10.230
Well...

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:20.700
Rackam?

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.210
Hey. Are you guys done now?

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.120
Yeah, for today.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.010
Hey, Gran...

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:36.880
Listen, where are we headed?

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:37.800
Huh?

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:41.100
Uh, rather, after we're done with the repairs.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:44.180
You still planning to head for
the Island of the Astrals?

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:48.230
The Island of the Astrals
is where my dad's waiting.

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:51.270
I have to go there.
That's the point of this journey.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:55.320
But that's not the only reason anymore.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:59.910
I also promised Lyria that
I'd take her there, no matter what.

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.080
What about you?

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:07.870
If there's anything that you want to do,
I'd be glad to help out.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:15.970
What are you talking about?

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:18.840
A kid your age needs to think
about his future first!

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:21.350
You've got a hell of a dream, right?

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:25.220
Then keep your eye on it,
and keep chasing after it.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.940
All right, I'm getting back to work now.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:36.820
There you go. I got it back for you.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.240
You did, indeed!

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.240
Thank you very much!

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:47.120
You took care of it with exceptional speed!

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:50.420
Just what I'd expect from a skyfarer
of your experience!

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:57.720
By the way, about that thing
I asked you to look into in Auguste...

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.970
Right, about that...

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:27.910
So as you can see, after Golonzo,
the trail has gone cold.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.750
Please forgive me!

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:32.580
No, that's more than I hoped for.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:36.920
Just finding out that they've been to this island...

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:45.550
Man, I'm hungry!

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:52.020
Food tastes even better
after a hard day's work, doesn't it?

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:54.900
Eugen hasn't come back yet?

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:57.320
Could it be that he's
not done with Siero's request?

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.650
He did say it was just an errand...

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:02.030
Here you go. This is on the house!

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:05.990
Thank you very much.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:07.790
We're grateful for your kindness.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.830
Hey, don't mention it.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:14.500
That little squirt, who couldn't drink anything
but milk, came back a grown man.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.840
So sure, I'm thrilled beyond words!

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:20.340
Hey, come on, enough of that!

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:25.510
Just look at you.
I'm so envious of you young guys.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.760
The sky's the limit.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:30.890
All you gotta do is
soar closer to your dream, huh?

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:57.210
This whole area here,
every part needs to be changed.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:01.800
Doesn't matter how much wear-and-tear,
just switch each one out with new ones.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.800
How'd the overhaul of
the auxiliary engine go?

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:09.100
You're good to go.
It's like brand-spanking new!

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:12.890
Then I guess we should load that one up first.

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:15.520
If all goes well, we could be done by today, huh?

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:20.020
Mr. Rackam! Is it alright
to remove this scaffolding now?

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:20.900
Sure!

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:24.150
Rackam, go grab something to eat while you can.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:27.990
When you're back, I want you to
do a final check of the power unit.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:28.910
Right.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:45.030
What is it that I want to do after this?

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:48.030
Why am I still on this journey?

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:01.210
A treat, did you say?

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:04.710
Yeah. I'm a little worried about Rackam.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:11.180
He's been kind of absent-minded lately,
and seems glum.

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:14.050
I thought if we could cheer him up even a little...

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:19.770
I get it! Everyone feels happy
when they eat something delicious!

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:21.850
I guess so, but...

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:26.360
Come to think of it, we don't know
a whole lot about Rackam's past, do we?

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:32.030
We did hear about how he's always wanted
to fly the Grandcypher.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:35.160
Mr. Rackam?

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:37.910
Please do the final check!

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:39.790
Sure, I'll be right there.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:55.350
Oh, this brings back memories...

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:57.770
I'm so glad that I got to see you again.

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.060
Grandcypher.

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:07.020
Siero!

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:11.530
Well, well! If it isn't Lyria and Gran!

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:13.780
Where are you going, Siero?

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:17.620
I have some business to attend to
in my office on the docks!

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:19.330
We're on our way to the docks, too.

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:24.170
We finished that job sooner than expected,
so we thought we'd help out with the repairs.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:27.920
I guess the work is going smoothly,
so they might not even need us anymore.

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:31.920
So the overhaul was "haulready" over, eh?

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:49.610
Rackam!

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:53.700
Oh, the smell of new parts and oil...

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:57.240
I see that you've repaired the Grandcypher.

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:00.740
You've made her look so beautiful...

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:04.500
Taking such pains,
right down to every nook and cranny.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:08.090
The furnace is in great condition, too.
It's moving so lightly.

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:12.210
I can sense just how eager she is
to take to the skies.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:17.340
You modified this part, didn't you?

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:21.600
It's a bit inelegant, but I think it will do.

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:23.600
Inelegant?

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:27.440
Yes. Though she seems to like it... the Grandcypher.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:30.360
Look how you've grown, Rackam.

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:34.740
Thank you...

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:39.240
For letting me see the Grandcypher again.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:42.660
H-Hey, hold up a second. Who are you?

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:47.370
I should have figured. You, too, I see.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.000
Me, too?

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:52.960
Hey, I'm not following you. Just what...

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:57.760
I'm sorry, I don't have time
to give you all the details now.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:01.390
This ship, the Grandcypher, is in imminent danger.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:03.470
What? Hey, what do you mean by—

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:04.730
We're back!

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:09.480
We're here to help you
with the Grandcypher's repairs!

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:21.490
Don't move!

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:23.450
I do say!

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:29.580
It's him!

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:32.210
You again?

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:38.630
I've had all that I can take
of this fruitless game of tag with you people!

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:42.390
However, today will mark the end
of said revelry, I do say!

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:44.600
Dark Essence!

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:48.190
Like I'd fall for the same trick...

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:55.190
Hey! What's wrong?

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:58.820
Stay away... Rackam...

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.290
Rackam!

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:23.680
Stop... it...

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:25.060
Stop it!

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:30.440
Now then! Reduce this annoying ship
to a pile of rubbish, on the double!

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:36.320
As the shipwright primal beast,
you must put your powers on full display!

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:38.030
Primal beast?

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:51.920
The Grandcypher!

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:56.710
It's exactly... the same...

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:16.270
<i>I'll make the Grandcypher fly myself,
no matter what!</i>

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:21.200
<i>And then I'll let you ride, too!</i>

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:22.530
<i>Noa!</i>

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:36.090
You... You're Noa?

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:53.640
Lyria!

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:56.230
His... voice is...

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:57.230
Hang in there!

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:06.200
Gran!

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:15.710
Dear me, you people truly are a handful!

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:21.840
But now we've successfully retrieved
the top secret girl, I do say!

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:24.720
Withdraw! Do you hear me?

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:26.550
I order you to pull out!

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:34.100
Noa!

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:40.190
Stop—

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:41.400
Out of the way!

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:46.530
I have no use for those people.
Just discard them!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.940
EPISODE 10
THE IMPOSSIBLE DREAM

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:38.600
Next episode, "The Impossible Dream"
